286
00:20:06,760 --> 00:20:09,720
(You're afraid you'll be the one to cross it and get close to me first.)

287
00:20:19,320 --> 00:20:20,800
I'm not afraid.

288
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,120
That line was about to break anyway.

289
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,120
I didn't think you'd come.

290
00:21:00,160 --> 00:21:01,920
Sit down. Come on.

291
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:04,400
Come on, have a seat.

292
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:07,080
Hey!

293
00:21:07,120 --> 00:21:08,960
Whoa, he's out.

294
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:14,256
You drink first. Here.

295
00:21:14,280 --> 00:21:15,576
Give it to Inspector Ken first.

296
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:16,297
Come on.

297
00:21:16,321 --> 00:21:18,800
Let's toast.

298
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:21,296
Can you down it?

299
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,880
Drink it all.

300
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:26,040
You drink too. I'm talking to you.

301
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:28,776
Come on, what are you doing?

302
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:30,936
- They're playing dance music!
- Hurry up!

303
00:21:30,960 --> 00:21:32,000
We have to film this.

304
00:21:32,040 --> 00:21:35,640
Go dance for us.

305
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:48,440
Wait, is anyone recording?

306
00:21:49,080 --> 00:21:51,160
Come on, cheers!

307
00:21:51,840 --> 00:21:54,200
Cheers!

308
00:21:59,240 --> 00:22:03,616
Keep drinking. Hey, you okay?

309
00:22:03,640 --> 00:22:04,936
Fluke's asleep. Who's paying?

310
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:06,296
Tammy?

311
00:22:06,320 --> 00:22:07,016
Tangme.

312
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:07,577
Huh?

313
00:22:07,601 --> 00:22:09,416
Tangme's pink.

314
00:22:09,440 --> 00:22:10,696
What do you mean, pink, Inspector?

315
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:12,880
- Where? What?
- Huh? What?

316
00:22:12,960 --> 00:22:14,136
- What are you talking about?
- What do you mean?

317
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:15,360
As for Inspector Ken...

318
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:21,256
Hey, can you still drink?

319
00:22:21,280 --> 00:22:23,056
- Why can't I see your color?
- I'm done.

320
00:22:23,080 --> 00:22:24,240
What?

321
00:22:24,320 --> 00:22:25,640
Come on, Phong. Drink.

322
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:27,680
Why?

323
00:22:28,360 --> 00:22:30,736
- Wait.
- No way.

324
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:33,640
Maybe I can't see it because you're not drunk yet.

325
00:22:35,760 --> 00:22:38,160
Then drink a little more.

326
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:38,697
Hey, sit down first.

327
00:22:38,721 --> 00:22:40,736
- Here, Inspector.
- Come sit down.

328
00:22:40,760 --> 00:22:41,896
Drink some more.

329
00:22:41,920 --> 00:22:43,360
I'm going to get wasted.

330
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:47,720
No one's leaving sober tonight. Cheers!

331
00:22:48,680 --> 00:22:49,960
As for Officer Phong...

332
00:22:52,560 --> 00:22:53,880
Green.

333
00:22:54,920 --> 00:22:55,497
Green.

334
00:22:55,521 --> 00:22:56,800
What green?

335
00:22:56,920 --> 00:22:58,760
What do you mean by green, Inspector?

336
00:22:58,800 --> 00:23:00,040
That's ridiculous.

337
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:03,056
- Hey, handsome. Can I get your contact?
- Inspector, look!

338
00:23:03,080 --> 00:23:05,456
- Add me.
- A girl's hitting on James.

339
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:06,520
My contact?

340
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:08,256
Contact info.

341
00:23:08,280 --> 00:23:09,800
My contact info.

342
00:23:10,760 --> 00:23:12,056
My contact info.

343
00:23:12,080 --> 00:23:13,960
- My contact info.
- Got a girlfriend?

344
00:23:14,080 --> 00:23:14,937
This is bad.

345
00:23:14,961 --> 00:23:16,960
What's wrong?

346
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:19,576
- Sorry.
- No chance. No chance.

347
00:23:19,600 --> 00:23:22,720
My friend's drunk. Now isn't a good time to ask.

348
00:23:24,160 --> 00:23:24,880
All right.

349
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:25,920
No chance.

350
00:23:26,320 --> 00:23:29,000
Absolutely no chance.

351
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:31,720
Did Special Investigation train you to hit on women?

352
00:23:32,800 --> 00:23:34,640
Stay out of it, Inspector.

353
00:23:34,760 --> 00:23:36,760
Since when are we friends?

354
00:23:37,480 --> 00:23:41,120
I don't even have your contact info.

355
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:47,160
Your contact. Give it to me.

356
00:23:47,280 --> 00:23:48,480
I don't have one.

357
00:23:48,760 --> 00:23:50,736
Then make an account.

358
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:52,480
What's so hard about that?

359
00:23:53,120 --> 00:23:55,000
Just create an account.

360
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:58,560
I want to send you stickers.

361
00:24:00,200 --> 00:24:01,680
What a headache.

362
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:04,400
Inspector.

363
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:09,280
Give me your contact info.

364
00:24:09,440 --> 00:24:10,217
What a headache.

365
00:24:10,241 --> 00:24:11,360
Ugh.

366
00:24:11,960 --> 00:24:12,777
Is he drunk?

367
00:24:12,801 --> 00:24:13,960
Hey, are you okay?

368
00:24:15,160 --> 00:24:16,376
Hey, Inspector.

369
00:24:16,400 --> 00:24:17,337
He's out. He's drunk.

370
00:24:17,361 --> 00:24:20,376
Get up. How'd you get so drunk? This is hilarious.

371
00:24:20,400 --> 00:24:21,736
Are you really this bad at drinking?

372
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:23,840
- Wake up.
- What a lightweight.

373
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:26,800
Quit pretending. You're a mess.

374
00:24:27,320 --> 00:24:29,680
You've drunk this much before. Why are you wasted today?

375
00:24:52,560 --> 00:24:53,640
Chita.

376
00:24:57,200 --> 00:24:58,200
Dr. Ji.

377
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:00,480
Uh

378
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:04,320
I wasn't sleeping on the job.

379
00:25:05,240 --> 00:25:06,760
Don't push yourself so hard.

380
00:25:07,720 --> 00:25:09,240
You should rest sometimes.

381
00:25:10,120 --> 00:25:11,200
Uh...

382
00:25:12,760 --> 00:25:14,360
You hardly ever sleep, Doctor.

383
00:25:15,640 --> 00:25:17,440
I want to improve too,

384
00:25:19,840 --> 00:25:21,840
so I hope you'll get more rest.

385
00:25:23,360 --> 00:25:25,696
If you collapse from exhaustion,

386
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:27,320
I wouldn't know what to do.

387
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:31,360
Your stitches are much better now.

388
00:25:34,520 --> 00:25:35,337
But I think

389
00:25:35,361 --> 00:25:37,760
this part still needs some work.

390
00:25:40,520 --> 00:25:41,720
Here?

391
00:25:42,240 --> 00:25:43,320
Yes. Here.

392
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:47,720
Take your time.

393
00:25:48,760 --> 00:25:50,896
This stitch needs to go deeper.

394
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:51,920
Hold it down.

395
00:25:52,000 --> 00:25:53,720
Press a little harder. Mm-hmm.

396
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:55,240
Very good.

397
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:05,280
Do the same on the other side.

398
00:26:10,880 --> 00:26:11,880
Chita.

399
00:26:12,680 --> 00:26:14,040
Chidtawan.

400
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:16,800
It sounds so bright.

401
00:26:17,600 --> 00:26:18,640
I like it.

402
00:26:20,200 --> 00:26:21,200
Thank you.

403
00:26:25,880 --> 00:26:27,000
But

404
00:26:29,520 --> 00:26:32,120
I wish my life were as bright as my name.

405
00:26:33,840 --> 00:26:35,200
What about Jirat?

406
00:26:36,160 --> 00:26:37,280
What does it mean?

407
00:26:39,600 --> 00:26:40,960
Jiratikarn.

408
00:26:42,640 --> 00:26:45,920
It means a long night.

409
00:26:46,360 --> 00:26:48,960
Maybe that's why I'm always spending nights with corpses.

410
00:26:49,640 --> 00:26:50,760
It feels like

411
00:26:51,600 --> 00:26:53,920
our names were switched.

412
00:27:03,600 --> 00:27:05,400
I believe that from now on,

413
00:27:05,760 --> 00:27:08,880
your life will keep getting brighter.

414
00:27:09,600 --> 00:27:11,880
The brightest part

415
00:27:12,680 --> 00:27:13,720
of my life right now

416
00:27:16,120 --> 00:27:17,680
is you, Dr. Ji.

417
00:27:30,920 --> 00:27:32,080
Ma'am.

418
00:27:34,360 --> 00:27:35,800
Where are you taking that blood bag?

419
00:27:46,000 --> 00:27:47,240
Ow!

420
00:27:53,640 --> 00:27:54,640
You...

421
00:27:57,400 --> 00:27:59,400
If you tell anyone about this,

422
00:28:00,760 --> 00:28:03,160
I'll make sure you're fired.

423
00:28:07,240 --> 00:28:08,320
Ow!

424
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:55,200
I remember

425
00:28:55,440 --> 00:28:58,320
you said you were color-blind.

426
00:29:01,760 --> 00:29:02,840
What color is this?

427
00:29:04,720 --> 00:29:05,720
Yellow.

428
00:29:13,360 --> 00:29:14,400
And this?

429
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:16,520
Green.

430
00:29:20,440 --> 00:29:21,520
What about that one?

431
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:24,200
Purple.

432
00:29:29,400 --> 00:29:30,400
And this?

433
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:38,560
Probably orange.

434
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:45,040
Didn't you say you were color-blind?

435
00:29:45,840 --> 00:29:47,560
How did you get them all right?

436
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:51,680
Being color-blind doesn't mean I don't know colors.

437
00:29:53,120 --> 00:29:54,480
Are you sober now?

438
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:55,960
Mm.

439
00:29:59,440 --> 00:30:01,640
So what does the world look like through your eyes?

440
00:30:02,560 --> 00:30:04,600
I'd love to see the world through your eyes.

441
00:30:08,360 --> 00:30:10,056
Your world is already beautiful.

442
00:30:10,080 --> 00:30:12,080
Why would you want to see mine?

443
00:30:13,560 --> 00:30:15,080
Are you sober now?

444
00:30:15,640 --> 00:30:16,056
Mm.

445
00:30:16,080 --> 00:30:17,080
Mm.

446
00:30:19,360 --> 00:30:20,800
Then let's go.

447
00:30:55,640 --> 00:30:58,640
I heard what you said at the bar.

448
00:30:59,720 --> 00:31:02,600
You told them we were friends, right?

449
00:31:03,440 --> 00:31:05,840
Friends should trust each other.

450
00:31:07,880 --> 00:31:09,800
When did I say I was your friend?

451
00:31:11,680 --> 00:31:13,240
You know,

452
00:31:14,160 --> 00:31:16,440
ever since I came to Nakhon Sawan,

453
00:31:17,120 --> 00:31:19,520
I've run into one strange thing after another.

454
00:31:20,360 --> 00:31:21,720
The case,

455
00:31:22,040 --> 00:31:23,440
the Nour...

456
00:31:24,760 --> 00:31:26,880
But the strangest thing is...

457
00:31:28,840 --> 00:31:30,600
You know,

458
00:31:32,520 --> 00:31:34,840
I don't just give you evidence.

459
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:37,680
I also have to teach you how to use social media.

460
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:41,000
I even protected you from Tee.

461
00:31:44,280 --> 00:31:45,280
This...

462
00:31:46,360 --> 00:31:47,600
Look.

463
00:31:48,320 --> 00:31:50,160
The wound still hasn't healed.

464
00:31:57,920 --> 00:32:02,320
Sexy, right?

465
00:32:10,080 --> 00:32:11,400
Put your shirt back on.

466
00:32:22,160 --> 00:32:24,920
♪ What a beautiful life ♪

467
00:32:25,880 --> 00:32:28,600
♪ How lucky I am ♪

468
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:35,440
♪ To hold your beautiful hands inside my own ♪

469
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:41,680
♪ Darling, when you look at me ♪

470
00:32:41,880 --> 00:32:44,616
♪ I forget how to breathe ♪

471
00:32:44,640 --> 00:32:49,600
♪ The noise around us fades into song ♪

472
00:32:50,920 --> 00:32:53,080
You're pretty cute too.

473
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:31,360
Your skin's so fair.

474
00:33:34,520 --> 00:33:39,080
Nakhon Sawan mochi.

475
00:33:41,040 --> 00:33:42,640
You talk nonsense when you're drunk.

476
00:33:58,800 --> 00:34:00,720
When are you making an online account?

477
00:34:10,600 --> 00:34:11,960
How do I sign up?

478
00:34:20,920 --> 00:34:21,920
Here.

479
00:34:23,600 --> 00:34:26,880
Now I can finally send you stickers.

480
00:34:36,840 --> 00:34:38,000
Happy now?

481
00:34:44,320 --> 00:34:46,760
One more thing, Inspector.

482
00:34:47,880 --> 00:34:49,600
Remember to join the group chat.

483
00:34:51,280 --> 00:34:53,480
Everyone's waiting for you.

484
00:35:13,560 --> 00:35:14,840
Oh, man.

485
00:35:15,240 --> 00:35:16,840
You're really bad at drinking.

486
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:19,720
Don't Bangkok folks drink herbal liquor?

487
00:35:20,280 --> 00:35:21,360
Inspector.

488
00:35:22,400 --> 00:35:23,440
Inspector.

489
00:35:24,160 --> 00:35:25,280
Inspector.

490
00:35:26,480 --> 00:35:27,680
Inspector.

491
00:35:30,280 --> 00:35:31,320
James.

492
00:35:38,480 --> 00:35:39,600
What is it, Phong?

493
00:35:39,680 --> 00:35:40,840
Something happened.

494
00:35:41,160 --> 00:35:42,936
A burned body was found in Chon Saeng Forest,

495
00:35:42,960 --> 00:35:45,640
with the same burns as Joe's wife.

496
00:35:47,440 --> 00:35:48,000
Let's go.

497
00:35:48,040 --> 00:35:49,040
Okay.

498
00:35:49,520 --> 00:35:50,680
Okay, okay.

499
00:35:59,800 --> 00:36:00,960
(Pathology Room)

500
00:36:01,800 --> 00:36:02,800
Chita, I...

501
00:36:09,320 --> 00:36:10,320
Chita.

502
00:36:22,840 --> 00:36:23,880
Eve.

503
00:36:23,960 --> 00:36:24,537
What is it?

504
00:36:24,561 --> 00:36:26,880
Didn't Chita come to work today?

505
00:36:27,080 --> 00:36:31,160
Chita called in sick today, Dr. Ji.

506
00:36:31,200 --> 00:36:32,800
Do you need him for something?

507
00:36:33,480 --> 00:36:34,160
Uh...

508
00:36:34,200 --> 00:36:35,376
No. Thanks.

509
00:36:35,400 --> 00:36:35,937
Okay.

510
00:36:35,961 --> 00:36:37,256
Um, excuse me.

511
00:36:37,280 --> 00:36:38,400
- Uh...
- What is it?

512
00:36:39,400 --> 00:36:41,320
Do you know where Chita lives?

513
00:36:41,800 --> 00:36:44,880
You need Chita's address? I'll send it to you later.

514
00:36:45,360 --> 00:36:45,856
Okay.

515
00:36:45,880 --> 00:36:46,880
Mm.

516
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:01,640
Chita.

517
00:37:03,040 --> 00:37:04,360
Chita, are you in there?

518
00:37:08,440 --> 00:37:10,280
I'm coming in.

519
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:31,040
Chita! Chita!

520
00:37:50,400 --> 00:37:51,760
Are you okay, Chita?

521
00:37:54,440 --> 00:37:56,080
I just have a slight fever.

522
00:38:02,680 --> 00:38:03,840
Wait here.

523
00:38:12,320 --> 00:38:13,320
Chita.

524
00:38:16,440 --> 00:38:17,640
I'll wipe you down.

525
00:39:47,880 --> 00:39:50,800
You smell like booze. Aren't you afraid of being investigated?

526
00:39:53,720 --> 00:39:55,176
Thanks for your concern,

527
00:39:55,200 --> 00:39:56,680
but I'm much better now.

528
00:39:58,480 --> 00:39:59,800
Did Tee do this?

529
00:40:00,280 --> 00:40:01,840
We can't be sure yet.

530
00:40:02,720 --> 00:40:04,320
We need to perform an autopsy first.

531
00:40:07,640 --> 00:40:09,480
The body was burned recently,

532
00:40:10,440 --> 00:40:12,040
so there may still be evidence.

533
00:40:13,560 --> 00:40:15,440
The suspect may still be nearby.

534
00:40:16,040 --> 00:40:17,320
If anything happens,

535
00:40:18,200 --> 00:40:19,480
I'll protect you.

536
00:40:19,600 --> 00:40:20,600
Okay?

537
00:40:21,240 --> 00:40:22,680
Can you really protect me?

538
00:40:23,320 --> 00:40:25,320
Of course. I'm strong enough.

539
00:40:29,520 --> 00:40:30,600
Zip up your jacket.

540
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:33,000
Hey, wait.

541
00:40:36,240 --> 00:40:37,240
Thank you

542
00:40:37,800 --> 00:40:39,560
for taking me back to the station last night.

543
00:40:40,600 --> 00:40:41,840
How did you know it was me?

544
00:40:43,240 --> 00:40:45,200
Because the last person with me

545
00:40:45,240 --> 00:40:46,240
was you.

546
00:40:53,360 --> 00:40:54,480
You kept clinging to me,

547
00:40:55,040 --> 00:40:56,320
so I had no choice.

548
00:40:57,360 --> 00:40:58,600
So

549
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:00,600
are you finally softening toward me?

550
00:41:38,480 --> 00:41:39,480
Inspector.

551
00:41:48,880 --> 00:41:49,960
What is it, Tangme?

552
00:41:51,160 --> 00:41:54,000
The team is taking the body for an autopsy.

553
00:42:15,600 --> 00:42:16,600
I'll wipe your back.

554
00:43:58,720 --> 00:44:00,720
I know you're almost fully recovered.

555
00:44:05,600 --> 00:44:06,720
I'm sorry, Doctor.

556
00:44:15,760 --> 00:44:17,680
My life used to feel empty.

557
00:44:21,360 --> 00:44:22,880
I just drifted through each day.

558
00:44:25,200 --> 00:44:26,520
Sometimes I know

559
00:44:28,000 --> 00:44:30,240
my leg may never be normal again.

560
00:44:35,920 --> 00:44:37,840
But whenever you look after me

561
00:44:39,560 --> 00:44:40,600
and examine my leg,

562
00:44:46,440 --> 00:44:48,560
I truly believe it can fully recover.

563
00:44:53,560 --> 00:44:55,600
That alone is enough

564
00:44:56,560 --> 00:44:58,080
to give me a reason to keep living.

565
00:44:59,120 --> 00:45:00,720
Get more rest from now on

566
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:04,120
so you'll recover faster.

567
00:45:06,480 --> 00:45:07,480
Okay.

568
00:45:09,080 --> 00:45:10,480
See you at the hospital.

569
00:45:16,080 --> 00:45:17,080
Here.

570
00:45:56,040 --> 00:45:57,040
Stop! Stop!

571
00:46:01,280 --> 00:46:02,280
Thanks.

572
00:46:06,880 --> 00:46:07,960
What's wrong with you?

573
00:46:08,160 --> 00:46:09,160
Huh?

574
00:46:09,560 --> 00:46:10,560
Jeez.

575
00:46:10,840 --> 00:46:12,080
Is our group falling apart?

576
00:46:12,480 --> 00:46:13,800
Look at what everyone's become.

577
00:46:14,960 --> 00:46:17,480
Having me here is like having the whole gang.

578
00:46:19,000 --> 00:46:20,080
Then don't you die on me.

579
00:46:21,120 --> 00:46:22,336
Stay with me, okay?

580
00:46:22,360 --> 00:46:23,840
Okay. I won't die.

581
00:46:24,680 --> 00:46:25,680
- I'm off.
- Go.

582
00:46:25,880 --> 00:46:26,640
See you.

583
00:46:26,680 --> 00:46:27,680
I'm off.

584
00:46:32,120 --> 00:46:33,120
Hey, Ji.

585
00:46:33,200 --> 00:46:34,200
Hi.

586
00:46:34,480 --> 00:46:35,480
Hello.

587
00:46:36,440 --> 00:46:37,560
Long day, bro?

588
00:46:38,160 --> 00:46:39,520
You're back late again.

589
00:46:42,360 --> 00:46:43,040
Hey, Nin.

590
00:46:43,240 --> 00:46:44,400
Close the door for me.

591
00:46:49,240 --> 00:46:50,240
Ow.

592
00:46:51,760 --> 00:46:52,760
What the hell?

593
00:47:01,920 --> 00:47:03,960
Do you have any other information about this body?

594
00:47:05,120 --> 00:47:08,040
This is no business for a kid. Go study.

595
00:47:12,840 --> 00:47:14,600
That tattoo matches my friend's.

596
00:47:20,200 --> 00:47:24,080
I'll find the case summary for you when I have time.

597
00:47:28,240 --> 00:47:30,640
Come on. Don't overthink it.

598
00:47:31,240 --> 00:47:32,177
Focus on your studies.

599
00:47:32,201 --> 00:47:35,000
(Police)

600
00:47:48,400 --> 00:47:49,400
Inspector.

601
00:47:49,800 --> 00:47:51,160
Find anything?

602
00:47:51,720 --> 00:47:53,600
The patrol team found nothing.

603
00:47:54,960 --> 00:47:57,160
I'm checking the other evidence too.

604
00:47:58,920 --> 00:48:02,360
Do you really think Tee did all of this?

605
00:48:03,360 --> 00:48:04,520
I'm not sure either.

606
00:48:04,840 --> 00:48:07,400
But if we can unlock that phone,

607
00:48:07,440 --> 00:48:09,200
we may find some clues.

608
00:48:09,560 --> 00:48:10,560
A phone?

609
00:48:11,000 --> 00:48:12,000
Whose?

610
00:48:13,760 --> 00:48:15,600
I found it at the scene this morning.

611
00:48:19,440 --> 00:48:20,816
I'll check the transformer.

612
00:48:20,840 --> 00:48:21,840
I'll go with you.

613
00:48:30,280 --> 00:48:31,680
Does the power go out often here?

614
00:48:31,840 --> 00:48:32,840
No.

615
00:48:35,120 --> 00:48:37,040
I'll check upstairs first.

616
00:48:37,240 --> 00:48:38,296
What floor is the transformer on?

617
00:48:38,320 --> 00:48:39,560
The top floor.

618
00:48:39,920 --> 00:48:40,960
I'll come with you.

619
00:48:41,640 --> 00:48:42,640
Ow!

620
00:48:43,240 --> 00:48:44,600
Who turned off the lights?

621
00:48:45,120 --> 00:48:46,120
Huh?

622
00:48:47,480 --> 00:48:49,560
Tangme! James!

623
00:48:51,520 --> 00:48:52,520
Hey!

624
00:48:53,080 --> 00:48:54,120
Who's there?

625
00:48:54,920 --> 00:48:55,920
Tangme!

626
00:48:57,120 --> 00:48:58,160
Hey, who's there?

627
00:48:58,440 --> 00:48:59,417
Who are you?

628
00:48:59,441 --> 00:49:01,080
Ah!

629
00:49:01,800 --> 00:49:02,920
Ow!

630
00:49:02,960 --> 00:49:03,976
Ow!

631
00:49:04,000 --> 00:49:05,320
Phong, what happened?

632
00:49:05,360 --> 00:49:07,800
Ow!

633
00:49:08,080 --> 00:49:08,977
Tangme!

634
00:49:09,001 --> 00:49:11,016
Take care of Phong. I'll chase the killer.

635
00:49:11,040 --> 00:49:12,040
Got it.

636
00:49:54,360 --> 00:49:55,480
You knew, didn't you?

637
00:50:07,720 --> 00:50:10,080
You knew about the Nour from the beginning.

638
00:50:11,960 --> 00:50:13,480
You never closed the case

639
00:50:14,480 --> 00:50:16,600
because you thought the killer was another Nour?

640
00:50:17,520 --> 00:50:18,520
Yes.

641
00:50:18,760 --> 00:50:21,360
I haven't reported it to HQ because I don't have any evidence yet.

642
00:50:22,960 --> 00:50:24,520
I'll go out and draw him out.

643
00:50:25,000 --> 00:50:26,280
Shoot when you can.

644
00:50:26,840 --> 00:50:28,440
Just don't hit him anywhere vital.

645
00:50:30,560 --> 00:50:31,760
What if I miss?

646
00:50:32,680 --> 00:50:33,760
I trust you.

647
00:50:50,160 --> 00:50:51,880
I know you're nearby.

648
00:50:54,440 --> 00:50:56,480
Are you one of the Nour who can kill their own kind?

649
00:51:06,080 --> 00:51:08,480
Hey! Are you okay?

650
00:51:10,120 --> 00:51:11,480
I saw you get hit.

651
00:51:35,080 --> 00:51:36,160
I'm sorry.

652
00:51:36,600 --> 00:51:38,200
I missed his vital areas,

653
00:51:38,720 --> 00:51:40,400
so he escaped with the evidence.

654
00:51:43,280 --> 00:51:44,280
It's okay.

655
00:51:44,920 --> 00:51:45,920
Thank you

656
00:51:46,200 --> 00:51:47,200
for trusting me.

657
00:51:52,360 --> 00:51:53,360
Hey.

658
00:51:55,760 --> 00:51:56,760
How did you do that?

659
00:52:08,960 --> 00:52:09,960
Ugh.

660
00:52:17,560 --> 00:52:21,000
Tangme called. Phong is much better, so don't worry.

661
00:52:23,080 --> 00:52:25,640
But why did the Nour come after this phone?

662
00:52:28,720 --> 00:52:30,760
I found it on the latest burned body.

663
00:52:31,160 --> 00:52:33,200
There must be evidence inside.

664
00:52:38,320 --> 00:52:39,320
Want some?

665
00:52:40,000 --> 00:52:41,400
No, thanks.

666
00:52:43,400 --> 00:52:44,600
You were right.

667
00:52:45,360 --> 00:52:47,160
Tee killed Mint.

668
00:52:47,280 --> 00:52:48,440
Tee is one of the Nour too.

669
00:52:49,040 --> 00:52:52,080
I'm gathering the evidence and getting my report ready to submit.

670
00:52:53,000 --> 00:52:54,400
Thank you for believing me.

671
00:52:56,920 --> 00:52:58,360
You've already hugged me.

672
00:52:58,880 --> 00:53:00,680
I shouldn't have gone soft on you.

673
00:53:05,080 --> 00:53:06,680
Why are you investigating this case?

674
00:53:08,320 --> 00:53:09,640
Because of your father's case?

675
00:53:11,240 --> 00:53:12,240
Yes.

676
00:53:12,840 --> 00:53:16,680
Now I'm certain one of the Nour killed my father.

677
00:53:17,480 --> 00:53:20,200
But I still don't know why.

678
00:53:21,400 --> 00:53:24,800
I won't let my father's death be in vain.

679
00:53:29,360 --> 00:53:30,920
I don't know if you remember,

680
00:53:31,640 --> 00:53:32,960
but we've met before.

681
00:53:36,320 --> 00:53:39,880
I felt the same when I first saw you at the hospital.

682
00:53:40,400 --> 00:53:41,680
Five years ago,

683
00:53:42,520 --> 00:53:43,840
at the laundromat.

684
00:53:52,240 --> 00:53:53,240
Ow.

685
00:54:13,680 --> 00:54:14,840
Oh.

686
00:54:15,680 --> 00:54:17,480
So you were the drenched guy that day.

687
00:54:17,960 --> 00:54:20,960
You even left your shoes behind. You were a mess.

688
00:54:23,040 --> 00:54:24,880
If you tell anyone about this,

689
00:54:25,240 --> 00:54:26,680
I'll arrest you.

690
00:54:27,840 --> 00:54:29,080
On what charge?

691
00:54:29,520 --> 00:54:31,840
For stopping you from climbing into a washing machine?

692
00:54:38,040 --> 00:54:40,680
But we've met before.

693
00:54:42,600 --> 00:54:44,800
That means I've known you for years.

694
00:54:45,720 --> 00:54:46,720
So

695
00:54:47,160 --> 00:54:48,760
can I cross that line now?

696
00:54:55,760 --> 00:54:57,160
Why do you insist on crossing it?

697
00:54:59,680 --> 00:55:01,440
Because I want to hear more of your stories.

698
00:55:09,920 --> 00:55:11,880
Then why have you been investigating the Nour?

699
00:55:12,520 --> 00:55:13,600
What are you really after?

700
00:55:14,640 --> 00:55:17,680
Like you, I want to catch the Nour behind these killings.

701
00:55:21,960 --> 00:55:23,720
So that means we

702
00:55:24,720 --> 00:55:26,440
have the same goal now, right?

703
00:55:32,360 --> 00:55:33,480
Then

704
00:55:35,040 --> 00:55:36,120
from now on,

705
00:55:37,600 --> 00:55:38,880
no matter what happens,

706
00:55:39,840 --> 00:55:41,520
I'll never hide anything from you.

707
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:44,120
And you

708
00:55:45,360 --> 00:55:47,160
can't hide anything from me either.

709
00:57:37,160 --> 00:57:38,440
They just won't quit, will they?

710
00:57:39,160 --> 00:57:40,600
I was just getting to the good part.

711
00:57:42,440 --> 00:57:43,440
Hello?

712
00:57:52,920 --> 00:57:53,960
I'm on my way.

713
00:57:58,960 --> 00:58:00,200
The burned body

714
00:58:01,000 --> 00:58:02,080
has been identified as Tee.

715
00:58:04,160 --> 00:58:08,640
=Nour= (A WeTV Original Series)

716
00:58:09,720 --> 00:58:12,600
(Case relationship chart)

717
00:59:25,480 --> 00:59:28,200
When are you going to fall for me?

718
00:59:42,400 --> 00:59:43,720
Inspector Ken.

719
00:59:47,240 --> 00:59:48,640
I like you.

720
00:59:51,000 --> 00:59:53,280
When will you feel the same?

721
00:59:58,680 --> 00:59:59,680
Inspector.

722
01:00:00,800 --> 01:00:01,880
I was joking.

723
01:00:02,600 --> 01:00:04,520
Who'd ever like you?
